          "text": "Rash"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Pink, blanching, non-itchy truncal rash appeared about 24 hours after the fever decreased, then spread to the neck and proximal limbs; now fading."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-9",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-9",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Associated reported symptoms"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Coryza. No cough, shortness of breath, or gastrointestinal symptoms. Oral intake okay. No mucosal involvement, blistering, arthralgia, or neurological red flags. Reports being a bit tired but otherwise feeling pretty well."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-10",
